   "id": "ketubot.110b.19",
   "daf": "110b",
   "sentenceId": 18,
   "he": "רַבָּן שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן גַּמְלִיאֵל אוֹמֵר: נוֹתֵן לָהּ מִמְּעוֹת קַפּוֹטְקְיָא. קָסָבַר כְּתוּבָּה דְּאוֹרָיְיתָא.",
   "en": "§ The mishna taught that «Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel says» that if one married a woman in Cappadocia and divorced her in Eretz Yisrael, «he» pays her the marriage contract «in the currency of Cappadocia.» The Gemara explains that Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel «holds» that «a marriage contract» applies «by Torah» law, which means that its debt must be paid according to its highest possible value. Consequently, one follows the place in which the obligation was formed, which is the halakha for all deeds and contracts, and there is no room for leniency in this matter."
  }
 ],
